### 1. Scaled-Up Web Infrastructure Description
This advanced architecture scales up and optimizes the infrastructure by decoupling/splitting the components onto dedicated servers, introducing a second load balancer for high availability, and separating the database tier.

- **Load Balancers (HAProxy 1 & HAProxy 2)**: Configured as a high-availability cluster (active-passive or active-active) to eliminate the load balancer single point of failure (SPOF) and distribute incoming traffic.
- **Web Servers (Dedicated Servers)**: Separate servers dedicated solely to handling incoming HTTP/HTTPS requests, serving static assets, and proxying dynamic requests.
- **Application Servers (Dedicated Servers)**: Separate servers running the application backend logic and code base, isolated from web serving and database storage.
- **Database Servers (Primary & Replica)**: Dedicated database servers ensuring that data processing, storage, and replication do not compete with web or application resource demands.

