### 2. Specifics & Explanations (Why Adding Each Element)
- **Why add a Second Load Balancer (HAProxy Cluster)?** 
  To eliminate the Single Point of Failure (SPOF) at the entry point of the network. If the primary load balancer fails, the secondary load balancer takes over seamlessly, ensuring continuous availability.
- **Why split components (Web Server, Application Server, Database) onto their own dedicated servers?** 
  - **Resource Isolation & Optimization**: Different tiers have different resource bottlenecks (e.g., databases are memory/I/O intensive, while web servers are network/CPU intensive). Isolating them prevents one component from starving another of CPU, RAM, or disk I/O.
  - **Independent Scalability**: You can scale each tier independently based on demand (e.g., adding more web servers without needing to replicate the entire stack).
  - **Enhanced Security and Maintainability**: Easier to manage configurations, apply targeted security policies, troubleshoot bottlenecks, and isolate failures to specific layers.
- **Why add more servers overall?** 
  To handle higher query-per-second (QPS) traffic loads, distribute processing overhead, and achieve true horizontal scalability and high availability across the entire stack.